  "answer": "The conditions required for Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) include:\n\n1. **Target Client Software**: The target must be a client that allows scripting communication from remote hosts, such as a JavaScript-enabled web browser.\n\n2. **Required Resources**: There must be the ability to deploy a custom hostile service that can be accessed by targeted clients, along with the capability to communicate synchronously or asynchronously with the client machine.\n\n3. **Required Skills**: \n   - High skill level is needed to exploit a client-side vulnerability to inject malicious scripts into the browser's executable process.\n   - A lower skill level may suffice for simpler attacks, such as placing a script in user-generated content sites (e.g., bulletin boards, blogs, wikis) that are echoed back to other client machines [Source 1][Source 2].",
